   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><span style=\"font:13px/normal Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;display:inline!important;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Hi,</span></div><div style=\"font:13px/normal Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px currentColor;text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;clear:both;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I am new to using ggplot (R plotting in general) and trying to create a Spider Plot with ggplot.</div><div style=\"font:13px/normal Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px currentColor;text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;clear:both;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">The best I could do looks like using the following code:</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">&gt; df=read.table(&quot;spaghettiPlotDataTest.tsv&quot;, header=T, sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)<br>&gt; str(df)<br>&#39;data.frame&#39;:   31 obs. of  3 variables:<br> $ Sample : int  1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 1 ...<br> $ Days   : int  0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 30 ...<br> $ Outcome: num  0.848 0.883 0.831 0.788 0.824 ...<br>&gt; <br>&gt; p = ggplot( df, aes( df$Days, df$Outcome, group=df$Sample ) ) +<br>+ geom_line(color=df$Sample)<br>&gt; p<br></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-right:1em;margin-left:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-If5KAzNhg6w/VsCXHMBCRVI/AAAAAAAAAAM/03p6aJIMNfM/s1600/SpiderPlotTest.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-If5KAzNhg6w/VsCXHMBCRVI/AAAAAAAAAAM/03p6aJIMNfM/s1600/SpiderPlotTest.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368245344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mH1G64JHdLvIbhKa33ZSE\"><img width=\"193\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-If5KAzNhg6w/VsCXHMBCRVI/AAAAAAAAAAM/03p6aJIMNfM/s200/SpiderPlotTest.jpg\" border=\"0\"></a></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">I am trying to get a legend on the right and also the following:</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"> - change x y labels<br> - circles or some other shape at the point where two different lines join.<br> - specify the thickness of the lines, different for different samples if possible.<br> - control the color of the lines, different for different samples groups if possible.</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">An example of what I am trying to achieve is given in Figure 2 of the following link:</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"http://cancergrace.org/cancer-treatments/2014/12/30/how-is-immunotherapy-administered-an-immunotherapy-primer-for-patients-pt-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cancergrace.org/cancer-treatments/2014/12/30/how-is-immunotherapy-administered-an-immunotherapy-primer-for-patients-pt-2/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368245345000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0MPymhg47coKXeauJa4FuM\">SpiderPlotExample</a></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">The full data set is attached.</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Thank you for your help.</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">- Pankaj</div><div style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
